## Working style — non-negotiables

1. **This repo is the system of record.** Every finding, data pull, report, and piece of
   stakeholder communication is tracked here. Not in a downloads folder, not in a chat
   thread, not only in someone's inbox. A file that lands outside gets moved in.

2. **Nothing goes loose at the root.** Every new file has a designated home at the moment
   it is created. If nothing fits, extend the structure deliberately rather than dropping
   it at root "for now".

3. **One running log per channel, never per-task files.** One section per item, newest
   first. Scattered per-task files are how a project loses its own history.

4. **Verify before you assert.** Any claim of the form "X was done", "X is pending", or "X
   is missing" is checked against an actual source — the CMS, the live page, the analytics
   platform, the tracker — never asserted from memory or carried over from last month's
   wording. This is the single most common way a report becomes wrong.

5. **Nothing ships without a review pass** against `DELIVERY_QUALITY_LEDGER.md`, done in
   writing. The deliverable is not finished until the ledger is updated with anything the
   review found.

6. **Never auto-send anything external.** Every outgoing message is presented in full and
   approved individually. A general go-ahead does not count.

7. **Regenerate, do not hand-patch.** Rendered outputs are built from their markdown
   source. Edit the source and re-render.

